From: XuanTie Linux SDK CI <noreply@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ndiff: import setuptools before distutils for Python 3.13

ndiff/setup.py imports distutils.* directly. Python 3.12 removed the
stdlib distutils package, so on python3 3.13 the ndiff build (invoked by
`python3 setup.py build` when PACKAGECONFIG[ndiff] is enabled) fails with:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'distutils'

Import setuptools before the distutils imports. setuptools ships a bundled
copy of distutils and, with SETUPTOOLS_USE_DISTUTILS=local (the default),
installs a meta path shim that makes `import distutils.*` resolve to
setuptools._distutils. This keeps setup.py working on Python 3.12+ while
remaining a no-op on older interpreters that still provide stdlib distutils.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nmap 7.80 is EOL; local py3.13 build fix]
---
--- a/ndiff/setup.py
+++ b/ndiff/setup.py
@@ -8,6 +8,11 @@
 
 from stat import *
 
+# On Python 3.12+ the stdlib distutils was removed; importing setuptools
+# first installs its bundled _distutils shim so the distutils.* imports
+# below resolve to setuptools._distutils.
+import setuptools  # noqa: F401
+
 import distutils.command
 import distutils.command.install
 import distutils.core
